translations.text:
Now, Laura, your window rests in sleep, though another age kept it awake, and the attentive threshold of your door no longer hears a lover's mad complaint;

for near night, after the morning of your childhood comes a frozen evening, spring withered, light dead, voice deserted, brow gray:

hang your mirror as an offering to Venus, where you see and mourn what you were in what you are; once sighed for, today you sigh.

Thus what neither others nor you wish to see, neither eyes nor your anger shall see, while you live old age and die to childhood.

Whoever would be cultured in a single day will learn the following jar-gon: splendors, arrogate, youth, foresees, candor, constructs, metric harmony;

little, much, otherwise, purple hue, neutrality, tramples, raises, mind, pulses, displays, release, adolescent, transfers signs, pyre, frustrates, harpy;

yields, prevents, caesuras, petulant, arena, sips, goal, silver, alternates, though a melodious rival dissolves.

Use plenty of liquid and wandering, a little nocturnal and cavern, and keep livor, hooked, and pore ready.

For all Castile already, with this primer alone, burns with Babylonian poets writing confused sonnets; and in La Mancha shepherds and farmhands, bellies stuffed with garlic, make cultured conceits like crumbs.
